{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat render-r1.txt; cat round46w-brief.md; ls gate-run19*; tail -20 mutants.log'","aggregated_output":"system 4373 characters; user 121246 characters; schema 9626 characters\nevidence items 237; themes 9\nsource passages the answer cites that the rendered request does not show: none\nschema errors: none\ncalc_check errors: none\nrecorded: [{\"type\": \"bridge\", \"figure\": \"q4f\", \"bridge\": \"carry\", \"alternate\": \"undetermined\"}]\nsame-base family (calls 8729, 8732): Relations: v35 rests on v14's base.\n# Council round 46w: after 46v (read-only, same thread)\n\n46v answered: opposing bounds (a lower and an upper bound meeting in one calculation) make the result 'mixed'. C2 refuses it (the value is unbounded; the judge must state an estimate). Any record of a mixed set uses the whole line, so it can only show possible crossings. R2m: '<3.5' with '>6.5' is refused by C2, and no definite crossing is recorded.\n\nGate run 19: 72 of 72. Mutants: 37 of 37 caught. render-r1 clean.\n\nAnswer GATE PASS STANDS or GATE FAIL, sorting any finding as (A) blocking or (B) a relabelling for the blind readers. Only (A) blocks. If no (A) remains, say GATE PASS STANDS.\ngate-run19.fixtures.json\ngate-run19.txt\nnumbers unchecked | G24nv | CAUGHT (['G24nv'])\nrung range unchecked | R1rneg | CAUGHT (['R1rneg', 'R1r6'])\nC6 ignores bounds | R4b2 | CAUGHT (['R4b2', 'R4b3', 'R4one'])\nminus sign ignored in bounds | R2b2b | CAUGHT (['R2b2a', 'R2b2b'])\noverlap alternate drops bounds | R2b1 | CAUGHT (['R2b1'])\nopposing bounds merged | R2m | CAUGHT (['R2m'])\nC3 off | R1a | CAUGHT (['R1a', 'R1qb'])\ncrossings ignore open ends | R4b3 | CAUGHT (['R4b3', 'R4one'])\nC3 bounds use paired ends | R1qc | CAUGHT (['R1qc'])\nC3 impossibility ignores open ends | R1qb | CAUGHT (['R1qb'])\nbounds dropped in recomputation | R4one | CAUGHT (['R4one'])\nC1 accepts any substring (alone) | T9 | CAUGHT (['T9'])\nC5 allows estimates | P3b | CAUGHT (['P3b'])\nper-unit identity ignores scope | P4 | CAUGHT (['P4'])\nper-unit inverse loses its scale | G3inv | CAUGHT (['G3inv'])\nC2 tolerance 50% | P2 | CAUGHT (['P2', 'U2'])\nbound direction ignored | R4m | CAUGHT (['R2b2b', 'R4m'])\nC9 same base off (both clauses) | G4m | CAUGHT (['G24m', 'G24d', 'G24c', 'G24x', 'G4x', 'G4c', 'G4m'])\nC10 prior not authenticated | P3c | CAUGHT (['P3c'])\nAll rules have a mutant; none is left unexercised.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
